<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Key Security Principles =
for Banking Workers:</strong></p>
<ol class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-decimal space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Data Minimization</stro=
ng>: Only send absolutely necessary data to workers</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Encryption in Transit</=
strong>: All worker communication encrypted</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Tokenization</strong>: =
Replace sensitive values with non-sensitive tokens</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Session-based Security<=
/strong>: Generate ephemeral keys per session</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Audit Everything</stron=
g>: Comprehensive logging for compliance</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Memory Clearing</strong=
>: Best-effort clearing of sensitive data</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>CSP Enforcement</strong=
>: Strict content security policies for workers</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>No Persistence</strong>=
: Workers cannot store data permanently</li>
</ol>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Additional Regulatory Co=
nsiderations:</strong></p>
<ul class=3D"[&amp;:not(:last-child)_ul]:pb-1 [&amp;:not(:last-child)_ol]:p=
b-1 list-disc space-y-1.5 pl-7">
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>SOX Compliance</strong>=
: All financial calculations must be auditable</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>PCI DSS</strong>: Credi=
t card data handling requirements</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>GDPR/CCPA</strong>: Cus=
tomer data privacy and right to deletion</li>
<li class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Basel III</strong>: Ris=
k calculation accuracy and traceability</li>
</ul>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">This approach ensures that even =
if workers are compromised, the exposure of sensitive customer data is mini=
mized through multiple layers of security controls.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: Ex=
ceptional answer! Your comprehensive approach to security in the worker con=
text really demonstrates the kind of security-first thinking we need at NAB=
.</p>
<h2 class=3D"text-xl font-bold text-text-100 mt-1 -mb-0.5">Interview Conclu=
sion</h2>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Interviewer</strong>: We=
've covered a lot of ground today, from the technical internals of JavaScri=
pt memory management to practical implementation of secure, scalable soluti=
ons for banking applications. Let me wrap up with one final question:</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words">Given everything we've discussed=
 about memory management, security, and performance optimization, how would=
 you approach <strong>mentoring a junior developer</strong> who is working =
on similar problems? What would be your strategy for helping them develop t=
he deep understanding needed for senior-level engineering at a bank like NA=
B?</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>Candidate</strong>: That=
's a fantastic question, and mentoring is something I'm really passionate a=
bout, especially in the banking context where the stakes are so high.</p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>My Mentoring Philosophy =
for Banking Engineers:</strong></p>
<p class=3D"whitespace-normal break-words"><strong>1. Build Understanding f=
rom First Principles</strong></p>
